    {
      "id": "Bs05RoDXj8Vb1gLoB0u6H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12,
      "y": -225,
      "width": 1035.95947265625,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1839132111,
      "version": 809,
      "versionNonce": 1573629537,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790260398889,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Database (PostGres)\n    - you'll need a server for this, and you'll have to give them the \"schema\"\n      to create and or update on every deploy.\n    - \"Schema-less\" (No-SQL) databases - MongoDb\n        - customers - {}, {...}, \n        - DO NOT SHARE THIS DATABASE WITH OTHER TEAMS\nParkingLot.Api\n    - A server somewhere? Maybe. A VM? Maybe. \n    - MOST likely delivered in a container.\n        - your API will be built into a container image\n\nAngular App\n    - the built application will have to go into a web server in each environment\n    - in local dev, the web server is Vite. You don't use that off of localhost. You need a \"real\" web server.\n    - Put the built app into a container with a web server we configure ourselves. (usually Nginx)\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Database (PostGres)\n    - you'll need a server for this, and you'll have to give them the \"schema\"\n      to create and or update on every deploy.\n    - \"Schema-less\" (No-SQL) databases - MongoDb\n        - customers - {}, {...}, \n        - DO NOT SHARE THIS DATABASE WITH OTHER TEAMS\nParkingLot.Api\n    - A server somewhere? Maybe. A VM? Maybe. \n    - MOST likely delivered in a container.\n        - your API will be built into a container image\n\nAngular App\n    - the built application will have to go into a web server in each environment\n    - in local dev, the web server is Vite. You don't use that off of localhost. You need a \"real\" web server.\n    - Put the built app into a container with a web server we configure ourselves. (usually Nginx)\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
